        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0058', 1, 'The speed distribution (km/h) is 20-25:13; 25-30:16; 30-35:21; 35-40:19; 40-45:9; 45-50:7. What speed is Q3, the value below which 75% of vehicles lie?', '38.4375', '38.618421052631575', '33.61842105263158', '51.776315789473685', 'b', 2, 'Use 3N/4 to locate Q3, then apply L+h/f(3N/4−c.f.).', 'N=85, so 3N/4=63.75. Q3 lies in 35-40; L=35, h=5, f=19, preceding c.f.=50. Q3=35+5/19(63.75−50)=38.62. Other options omit c.f., change f to f+1, or subtract the current class frequency too.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0059', 1, 'The speed distribution (km/h) is 20-25:10; 25-30:17; 30-35:22; 35-40:16; 40-45:10; 45-50:6. What speed is Q3, the value below which 75% of vehicles lie?', '38.671875', '33.671875', '38.455882352941174', '53.984375', 'a', 2, 'Use 3N/4 to locate Q3, then apply L+h/f(3N/4−c.f.).', 'N=81, so 3N/4=60.75. Q3 lies in 35-40; L=35, h=5, f=16, preceding c.f.=49. Q3=35+5/16(60.75−49)=38.67. Other options omit c.f., change f to f+1, or subtract the current class frequency too.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0060', 1, 'The speed distribution (km/h) is 20-25:11; 25-30:18; 30-35:23; 35-40:17; 40-45:8; 45-50:7. What speed is Q3, the value below which 75% of vehicles lie?', '53.529411764705884', '38.23529411764706', '38.05555555555556', '33.23529411764706', 'b', 2, 'Use 3N/4 to locate Q3, then apply L+h/f(3N/4−c.f.).', 'N=84, so 3N/4=63. Q3 lies in 35-40; L=35, h=5, f=17, preceding c.f.=52. Q3=35+5/17(63−52)=38.24. Other options omit c.f., change f to f+1, or subtract the current class frequency too.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0061', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:3, 10-20:5, 20-30:x, 30-40:2, 40-50:0, Q2 is 22. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-4.285714285714286', '-7.5', '10', '-15.0', 'c', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=10+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=8, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−8)=22 gives x=10. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 8+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0062', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:4, 10-20:4, 20-30:x, 30-40:3, 40-50:-1, Q2 is 23. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-10.0', '-3.75', '15', '-3.3333333333333335', 'c', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=10+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=8, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−8)=23 gives x=15. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 8+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0063', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:5, 10-20:3, 20-30:x, 30-40:2, 40-50:2, Q2 is 21. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-20.0', '-10.0', '5', '-3.3333333333333335', 'c', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=12+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=8, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−8)=21 gives x=5. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 8+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0064', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:6, 10-20:2, 20-30:x, 30-40:3, 40-50:2, Q2 is 22. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-2.5', '5', '-2.142857142857143', '-7.5', 'b', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=13+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=8, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−8)=22 gives x=5. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 8+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0065', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:3, 10-20:6, 20-30:x, 30-40:2, 40-50:1, Q2 is 22. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-7.5', '-15.0', '10', '-4.285714285714286', 'c', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=12+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=9, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−9)=22 gives x=10. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 9+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0066', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:4, 10-20:5, 20-30:x, 30-40:3, 40-50:0, Q2 is 23. Determine the missing frequency x.', '15', '-10.0', '-3.75', '-3.3333333333333335', 'a', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=12+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=9, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−9)=23 gives x=15. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 9+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0067', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:5, 10-20:5, 20-30:x, 30-40:2, 40-50:0, Q2 is 21. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-20.0', '-40.0', '-6.666666666666667', '10', 'd', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=12+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=10, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−10)=21 gives x=10. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 10+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0068', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:6, 10-20:4, 20-30:x, 30-40:3, 40-50:-1, Q2 is 23. Determine the missing frequency x.', '20', '-5.0', '-13.333333333333334', '-4.444444444444445', 'a', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=12+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=10, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−10)=23 gives x=20. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 10+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0069', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:3, 10-20:7, 20-30:x, 30-40:2, 40-50:2, Q2 is 22. Determine the missing frequency x.', '-15.0', '-4.285714285714286', '-7.5', '10', 'd', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=14+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=10, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−10)=22 gives x=10. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 10+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0070', 1, 'In the distribution 0-10:4, 10-20:8, 20-30:x, 30-40:3, 40-50:1, Q2 is 23. Determine the missing frequency x.', '20', '-4.444444444444445', '-13.333333333333334', '-5.0', 'a', 3, 'Represent N and the missing class frequency with x, then substitute into the grouped Q2 formula.', 'Let N=16+x. For 20-30, L=20, h=10, preceding c.f.=12, and f=x. Substitution into Q2=20+10/x(N/2−12)=23 gives x=20. The other options arise from treating the preceding c.f. as 12+x, forgetting x in N, or replacing x by a known frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0071', 1, 'A distribution of 40 shops has frequencies 0-10:2, 10-20:a, 20-30:10, 30-40:10, 40-50:b. If Q1=25, find a and b.', 'a=5, b=13', 'a=15, b=3', 'a=1, b=17', 'a=3, b=15', 'd', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=18. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 25=20+10/10(40/4−(2+a)), giving a=3; hence b=15. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0072', 1, 'A distribution of 40 shops has frequencies 0-10:2, 10-20:a, 20-30:12, 30-40:12, 40-50:b. If Q1=24.17, find a and b.', 'a=3, b=11', 'a=11, b=3', 'a=1, b=13', 'a=5, b=9', 'a', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=14. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 24.17=20+10/12(40/4−(2+a)), giving a=3; hence b=11. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0073', 1, 'A distribution of 40 shops has frequencies 0-10:2, 10-20:a, 20-30:18, 30-40:6, 40-50:b. If Q1=22.78, find a and b.', 'a=11, b=3', 'a=3, b=11', 'a=5, b=9', 'a=1, b=13', 'b', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=14. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 22.78=20+10/18(40/4−(2+a)), giving a=3; hence b=11. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0074', 1, 'A distribution of 40 shops has frequencies 0-10:3, 10-20:a, 20-30:14, 30-40:10, 40-50:b. If Q1=22.14, find a and b.', 'a=9, b=4', 'a=4, b=9', 'a=6, b=7', 'a=2, b=11', 'b', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=13. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 22.14=20+10/14(40/4−(3+a)), giving a=4; hence b=9. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0075', 1, 'A distribution of 40 shops has frequencies 0-10:4, 10-20:a, 20-30:14, 30-40:10, 40-50:b. If Q1=20.71, find a and b.', 'a=5, b=7; alternative 1', 'a=7, b=5', 'a=5, b=7', 'a=3, b=9', 'c', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=12. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 20.71=20+10/14(40/4−(4+a)), giving a=5; hence b=7. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0076', 1, 'A distribution of 44 shops has frequencies 0-10:3, 10-20:a, 20-30:18, 30-40:8, 40-50:b. If Q1=22.78, find a and b.', 'a=12, b=3', 'a=1, b=14', 'a=5, b=10', 'a=3, b=12', 'd', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=15. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 22.78=20+10/18(44/4−(3+a)), giving a=3; hence b=12. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0077', 1, 'A distribution of 48 shops has frequencies 0-10:3, 10-20:a, 20-30:14, 30-40:10, 40-50:b. If Q1=20.71, find a and b.', 'a=6, b=15', 'a=8, b=13', 'a=13, b=8', 'a=10, b=11', 'b', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=21. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 20.71=20+10/14(48/4−(3+a)), giving a=8; hence b=13. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0078', 1, 'A distribution of 52 shops has frequencies 0-10:2, 10-20:a, 20-30:16, 30-40:8, 40-50:b. If Q1=24.38, find a and b.', 'a=4, b=22', 'a=22, b=4', 'a=2, b=24', 'a=6, b=20', 'a', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=26. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 24.38=20+10/16(52/4−(2+a)), giving a=4; hence b=22. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0079', 1, 'A distribution of 56 shops has frequencies 0-10:2, 10-20:a, 20-30:10, 30-40:6, 40-50:b. If Q1=24, find a and b.', 'a=6, b=32', 'a=30, b=8', 'a=10, b=28', 'a=8, b=30', 'd', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=38. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 24=20+10/10(56/4−(2+a)), giving a=8; hence b=30. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0080', 1, 'A distribution of 60 shops has frequencies 0-10:2, 10-20:a, 20-30:10, 30-40:6, 40-50:b. If Q1=24, find a and b.', 'a=9, b=33', 'a=33, b=9', 'a=7, b=35', 'a=11, b=31', 'a', 3, 'Form one equation from total frequency and a second from the Q1 formula.', 'From total frequency, a+b=42. Since Q1 lies in 20-30, 24=20+10/10(60/4−(2+a)), giving a=9; hence b=33. The distractors swap the missing frequencies or change a by 2, which violates the total or quartile equation.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0081', 1, 'The ordered data are 120, 140, 160, 171, 191, 211, 222, 242. Find D3.', '154.0', '160', '148.0', '140', 'a', 2, 'Use i(n+1)/10; interpolate if the position is fractional.', 'Position of D3 = 3(n+1)/10 = 2.7th. Interpolate between 140 and 160 to get 154. The distractors result from omitting the +1, taking the lower observation only, or taking the upper observation only.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0082', 1, 'The ordered data are 131, 151, 171, 182, 202, 222, 233, 253, 273. Find P7.', '131', '174.60000000000002', '173.60000000000002', '183.54000000000002', 'c', 2, 'Use i(n+1)/100; interpolate if the position is fractional.', 'Position of P7 = 7(n+1)/100 = 0.7th. Interpolate between 273 and 131 to get 173.6. The distractors result from omitting the +1, taking the lower observation only, or taking the upper observation only.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0083', 1, 'The ordered data are 142, 162, 182, 193, 213, 233, 244, 264, 284, 295. Find D2.', '162', '166.0', '182', '167.0', 'b', 2, 'Use i(n+1)/10; interpolate if the position is fractional.', 'Position of D2 = 2(n+1)/10 = 2.2th. Interpolate between 162 and 182 to get 166. The distractors result from omitting the +1, taking the lower observation only, or taking the upper observation only.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0084', 1, 'The ordered data are 153, 173, 193, 204, 224, 244, 255, 275, 295, 306, 326. Find P5.', '223.2', '222.2', '230.85', '153', 'b', 2, 'Use i(n+1)/100; interpolate if the position is fractional.', 'Position of P5 = 5(n+1)/100 = 0.6th. Interpolate between 326 and 153 to get 222.2. The distractors result from omitting the +1, taking the lower observation only, or taking the upper observation only.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0085', 1, 'The ordered data are 164, 184, 204, 215, 235, 255, 266, 286, 306, 317, 337, 357. Find D4.', '255', '239.0', '231.0', '235', 'b', 2, 'Use i(n+1)/10; interpolate if the position is fractional.', 'Position of D4 = 4(n+1)/10 = 5.2th. Interpolate between 235 and 255 to get 239. The distractors result from omitting the +1, taking the lower observation only, or taking the upper observation only.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0086', 1, 'The ordered data are 175, 195, 215, 226, 246, 266, 277, 297, 317, 328, 348, 368, 379. Find P6.', '207.64000000000001', '219.88', '175', '208.64000000000001', 'a', 2, 'Use i(n+1)/100; interpolate if the position is fractional.', 'Position of P6 = 6(n+1)/100 = 0.84th. Interpolate between 379 and 175 to get 207.64. The distractors result from omitting the +1, taking the lower observation only, or taking the upper observation only.'),
