        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0140', 1, 'In an examination with the grouped marks 0-10:5, 10-20:10, 20-30:20, 30-40:21, 40-50:12, 50-60:5, 42% of students pass. Estimate the minimum passing mark.', '33.336363636363636', '33.49523809523809', '23.495238095238097', '50.161904761904765', 'b', 3, 'The failed percentage gives the percentile at the pass cutoff; compute that percentile using grouped data.', 'If 42% pass, 58% fail, so the cutoff is P58. Its rank is 58N/100=42.34. It lies in 30-40; therefore cutoff=30+10/21(42.34−35)=33.5. The other options come from omitting c.f., changing f, or subtracting the class frequency.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0141', 1, 'A grouped age distribution has frequencies 20-30:70, 30-40:120, 40-50:160, 50-60:80. What percentage of workers are older than 35 years?', '55.81395348837209', '83.72093023255815', '30.232558139534884', '69.76744186046511', 'd', 3, 'Locate the class containing the given age and divide that class proportionally at the given value.', '35 lies in 30-40. Estimate the proportion below it as [c.f. + f(35−30)/10]/N ×100 = [70+120(35−30)/10]/430×100 = 30.23%. Hence the percentage above 35 is 100−30.23=69.77%. The distractors use the below percentage directly, stop at the preceding class, or count the whole target class.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0142', 1, 'A grouped age distribution has frequencies 20-30:71, 30-40:121, 40-50:161, 50-60:81. What percentage of workers are older than 37 years?', '35.875576036866356', '64.12442396313364', '83.6405529953917', '55.76036866359447', 'b', 3, 'Locate the class containing the given age and divide that class proportionally at the given value.', '37 lies in 30-40. Estimate the proportion below it as [c.f. + f(37−30)/10]/N ×100 = [71+121(37−30)/10]/434×100 = 35.88%. Hence the percentage above 37 is 100−35.88=64.12%. The distractors use the below percentage directly, stop at the preceding class, or count the whole target class.'),
