        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0154', 1, 'For classes 0-10, 10-20, 20-30, 30-40 and 40-50, the frequencies are 5, x, 10, 4, 2. If D2=11.3333, find x.', '18.0', '10', '14', '12', 'd', 3, 'Write N in terms of x and use D2=L+h/f(2N/10−c.f.).', 'Total N=21+x. Since D2 is in 10-20, D2=10+10/x[N/5−5]=11.33. Solving gives x=12. Option A (18.0) results from an algebraic shift such as using the wrong class-position factor or moving a term incorrectly. Option B (10) results from an algebraic shift such as using the wrong class-position factor or moving a term incorrectly. Option C (14) results from an algebraic shift such as using the wrong class-position factor or moving a term incorrectly.'),
