        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0165', 1, 'A less-than ogive is being used for a grouped distribution containing N=80 observations. To locate Q3 graphically, what cumulative-frequency value should be marked on the Y-axis before drawing the horizontal line?', '64.0', '40.0', '60.0', '20.0', 'c', 1, 'For a quartile use iN/4, for a decile iN/10, and for a percentile iN/100.', 'For a graphical partition value, use the corresponding cumulative-frequency level. For Q3, the level is 60. The other options use a different partition fraction, such as N/2, N/4, 8N/10 or 6N/10.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0166', 1, 'A less-than ogive is being used for a grouped distribution containing N=90 observations. To locate D4 graphically, what cumulative-frequency value should be marked on the Y-axis before drawing the horizontal line?', '36.0', '22.5', '72.0', '45.0', 'a', 1, 'For a quartile use iN/4, for a decile iN/10, and for a percentile iN/100.', 'For a graphical partition value, use the corresponding cumulative-frequency level. For D4, the level is 36. The other options use a different partition fraction, such as N/2, N/4, 8N/10 or 6N/10.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0167', 1, 'A less-than ogive is being used for a grouped distribution containing N=100 observations. To locate D7 graphically, what cumulative-frequency value should be marked on the Y-axis before drawing the horizontal line?', '70.0', '50.0', '25.0', '80.0', 'a', 1, 'For a quartile use iN/4, for a decile iN/10, and for a percentile iN/100.', 'For a graphical partition value, use the corresponding cumulative-frequency level. For D7, the level is 70. The other options use a different partition fraction, such as N/2, N/4, 8N/10 or 6N/10.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0168', 1, 'A less-than ogive is being used for a grouped distribution containing N=110 observations. To locate P25 graphically, what cumulative-frequency value should be marked on the Y-axis before drawing the horizontal line?', '27.5', '55.0', '88.0', '66.0', 'a', 1, 'For a quartile use iN/4, for a decile iN/10, and for a percentile iN/100.', 'For a graphical partition value, use the corresponding cumulative-frequency level. For P25, the level is 27.5. The other options use a different partition fraction, such as N/2, N/4, 8N/10 or 6N/10.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0169', 1, 'A less-than ogive is being used for a grouped distribution containing N=120 observations. To locate P75 graphically, what cumulative-frequency value should be marked on the Y-axis before drawing the horizontal line?', '90.0', '60.0', '96.0', '30.0', 'a', 1, 'For a quartile use iN/4, for a decile iN/10, and for a percentile iN/100.', 'For a graphical partition value, use the corresponding cumulative-frequency level. For P75, the level is 90. The other options use a different partition fraction, such as N/2, N/4, 8N/10 or 6N/10.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0170', 1, 'A less-than ogive is being used for a grouped distribution containing N=130 observations. To locate P50 graphically, what cumulative-frequency value should be marked on the Y-axis before drawing the horizontal line?', '65.0', '78.0', '32.5', '104.0', 'a', 1, 'For a quartile use iN/4, for a decile iN/10, and for a percentile iN/100.', 'For a graphical partition value, use the corresponding cumulative-frequency level. For P50, the level is 65. The other options use a different partition fraction, such as N/2, N/4, 8N/10 or 6N/10.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0171', 1, 'Discontinuous classes are 10-14, 15-19, 20-24. What lower class boundary should be used when converting the first class to a continuous interval?', '65.0', '78.0', '32.5', '104.0', 'a', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'The gap between successive class limits is 1, so subtract 0.5 from the first lower limit. The continuous lower boundary is 9.5. The alternatives retain the discontinuous limit, add 0.5, or subtract 1.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0172', 1, 'For the same style of discontinuous classes 11-15, 16-20, 21-25, what upper boundary corresponds to the first class after making the classes continuous?', '65.0', '78.0', '32.5', '104.0', 'a', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'Add 0.5 to the upper class limit 15, giving 15.5. The alternatives leave the class unchanged or shift it by a full unit.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0173', 1, 'A less-than ogive for N=60 employees is drawn. What Y-axis level should be used to locate the median?', '31.0', '42.0', '30.0', '15.0', 'c', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'The required Y-axis level is 30. The other options use a different partition fraction.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0174', 1, 'A less-than ogive represents N=65 observations. What cumulative-frequency level locates Q1?', '32.5', '17.25', '16.25', '45.5', 'c', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'The required Y-axis level is 16.25. The other options use a different partition fraction.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0175', 1, 'A less-than ogive represents N=70 observations. At what Y-axis level should D7 be located?', '17.5', '50.0', '49.0', '35.0', 'c', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'The required Y-axis level is 49. The other options use a different partition fraction.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0176', 1, 'A less-than ogive represents N=75 observations. At what cumulative-frequency level should P70 be located?', '52.5', '37.5', '53.5', '18.75', 'a', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'The required Y-axis level is 52.5. The other options use a different partition fraction.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0177', 1, 'Discontinuous classes 16-20, 21-25 are converted to continuous classes. Which interval is correct for the first class?', '(15.5, 21.5)', '(16, 20)', '(16.5, 20.5)', '(15.5, 20.5)', 'd', 2, 'Make discontinuous classes continuous by adjusting each boundary by half the gap.', 'With a gap of 1, subtract 0.5 from the lower limit and add 0.5 to the upper limit. The first continuous interval is 15.5-20.5.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0178', 1, 'An ogive for 100 employees shows that the horizontal line at cumulative frequency 18 meets the curve at approximately x=18. What does the graph estimate about the number of employees below 18 hours?', '25.0', '52.5', '70.0', '50.0', 'b', 2, 'Use the appropriate cumulative-frequency level; for discontinuous classes, first make the class boundaries continuous.', 'The required Y-axis level is 52.5. The other options use a different partition fraction.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0179', 1, 'A less-than ogive for N=80 has the horizontal line y=40 meeting the curve at x≈33. What partition value does this represent?', 'Q1', 'P60', 'Q2 (median)', 'D8', 'c', 2, 'Compare the Y-axis level with N/2, N/4, iN/10 or iN/100.', 'Since y=N/2=40, the partition value is Q2, the median. Q1 would use N/4, D8 would use 8N/10, and P60 would use 60N/100.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0180', 1, 'A less-than ogive for N=120 observations shows x=39 at cumulative frequency 72. Which percentile is located there?', 'P50', 'D6', 'P60', 'P75', 'c', 2, 'Convert the cumulative frequency at the point into a percentage of N.', '72/120×100=60, so the point represents P60. The alternatives correspond to different cumulative percentages.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0181', 1, 'The ordered data are 12, 18, 25, 31, 44, 50. What is the median?', '25', '29.5', '31', '28', 'b', 1, 'Recall the definition or formula directly, then substitute the given values if needed.', 'F Option A uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option C uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option D uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option A applies the wrong definition or formula. Option C applies the wrong definition or formula. Option D applies the wrong definition or formula.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0182', 1, 'A data set is divided into 5 equal parts. How many observations are represented by each part when there are 100 observations?', '5', '25', '20', '50', 'c', 1, 'Recall the definition or formula directly, then substitute the given values if needed.', 'a Option A uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option B uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option D uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option A applies the wrong definition or formula. Option B applies the wrong definition or formula. Option D applies the wrong definition or formula.'),
        ('mth11b-01-mcq-0183', 1, 'If Q1=32 for an ordered data set, what percentage of observations lie below Q1?', '25%', '75%', '20%', '50%', 'a', 1, 'Recall the definition or formula directly, then substitute the given values if needed.', 'Option B uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option C uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option D uses a different definition, formula, or axis choice. Option B applies the wrong definition or formula. Option C applies the wrong definition or formula. Option D applies the wrong definition or formula.'),
