        ('mth11b-06-mcq-0221', 6, 'Find n if 8P5 = 20 × nP3.', '8', '5', '7', '23', 'a', 2, 'Cancel the common nPr factors, then solve the resulting product of two consecutive integers.', '8P5/8P3 = (5)(4) = 5×4 = 20; hence n−r=5 and n=8. Option B results from using combinations, which ignore order. Option C results from allowing repetition when it is forbidden. Option D results from using an incomplete permutation product.'),
