        ('mth11b-06-mcq-0224', 6, 'Find n if 12P7 = 42 × nP5.', '11', '12', '47', '7', 'b', 2, 'Cancel the common nPr factors, then solve the resulting product of two consecutive integers.', '12P7/12P5 = (7)(6) = 7×6 = 42; hence n−r=7 and n=12. Option A results from using combinations, which ignore order. Option C results from allowing repetition when it is forbidden. Option D results from using an incomplete permutation product.'),
