        ('mth11b-06-mcq-0301', 6, 'Given nC(r−1) : nCr : nC(r+1) = 21 : 14 : 6, find n and r.', 'n=6, r=9', 'n=10, r=6', 'n=9, r=7', 'n=9, r=6', 'd', 2, 'Use nC(r−1)/nCr = r/(n−r+1) and nCr/nC(r+1) = (r+1)/(n−r).', 'From the first ratio, r/(n−r+1) = 21/14; from the second, (r+1)/(n−r) = 14/6. Solving gives n=9, r=6. Option A results from using permutations, which count order. Option B results from using the wrong complementary or adjacent index. Option C results from an arithmetic slip after applying the combination identity.'),
