        ('mth11b-07-mcq-0010', 7, 'The experiment consists of tossing a coin and a nine-sided die labeled 1–9. Which set correctly represents its sample space?', '{(1,H), (1,T)}', '9/7', '{(H,1), (T,1)}', '{(H,1)}', 'c', 1, 'List every possible coin result with every possible die result.', '1. There are 2 coin outcomes and 1 die outcomes.
2. Pair each coin outcome with each die outcome, giving 2×1 ordered outcomes.

Wrong-option checks: Option A: reverses the ordered positions of the coin and die; Option B: results from an arithmetic or counting error; Option D: omits one tail outcome'),
        ('mth11b-07-mcq-0011', 7, 'A traveler can reach a destination by bus, train, or flight. After arriving, a local tour can be completed by metro or taxi. Which set lists all combined outcomes?', '{(bus, bus), (bus, train), (train, bus), (train, train), (flight, bus), (flight, train)}', '{(bus, metro), (bus, taxi), (train, metro), (train, taxi), (flight, metro), (flight, taxi)}', '{(bus, metro), (bus, taxi), (train, metro), (train, taxi)}', '{(bus, metro), (train, metro), (flight, metro)}', 'b', 1, 'Combine each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.', '1. There are 3 first-stage choices and 2 second-stage choices.
2. The combined outcomes are the six ordered pairs formed by taking each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.

Wrong-option checks: Option A: uses travel methods as if they were local-tour choices; Option C: omits all outcomes using the third travel method; Option D: omits the second local-tour choice for every route'),
        ('mth11b-07-mcq-0012', 7, 'A traveler can reach a destination by car, train, or boat. After arriving, a local tour can be completed by bus or cab. Which set lists all combined outcomes?', '{(car, bus), (car, cab), (train, bus), (train, cab)}', '{(car, bus), (train, bus), (boat, bus)}', '{(car, car), (car, train), (train, car), (train, train), (boat, car), (boat, train)}', '{(car, bus), (car, cab), (train, bus), (train, cab), (boat, bus), (boat, cab)}', 'd', 1, 'Combine each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.', '1. There are 3 first-stage choices and 2 second-stage choices.
2. The combined outcomes are the six ordered pairs formed by taking each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.

Wrong-option checks: Option A: omits all outcomes using the third travel method; Option B: omits the second local-tour choice for every route; Option C: uses travel methods as if they were local-tour choices'),
        ('mth11b-07-mcq-0013', 7, 'A traveler can reach a destination by bike, coach, or plane. After arriving, a local tour can be completed by tram or taxi. Which set lists all combined outcomes?', '{(bike, tram), (coach, tram), (plane, tram)}', '{(bike, bike), (bike, coach), (coach, bike), (coach, coach), (plane, bike), (plane, coach)}', '{(bike, tram), (bike, taxi), (coach, tram), (coach, taxi)}', '{(bike, tram), (bike, taxi), (coach, tram), (coach, taxi), (plane, tram), (plane, taxi)}', 'd', 1, 'Combine each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.', '1. There are 3 first-stage choices and 2 second-stage choices.
2. The combined outcomes are the six ordered pairs formed by taking each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.

Wrong-option checks: Option A: omits the second local-tour choice for every route; Option B: uses travel methods as if they were local-tour choices; Option C: omits all outcomes using the third travel method'),
        ('mth11b-07-mcq-0014', 7, 'A traveler can reach a destination by ferry, train, or car. After arriving, a local tour can be completed by bus or rickshaw. Which set lists all combined outcomes?', '{(ferry, bus), (ferry, rickshaw), (train, bus), (train, rickshaw)}', '{(ferry, bus), (train, bus), (car, bus)}', '{(ferry, bus), (ferry, rickshaw), (train, bus), (train, rickshaw), (car, bus), (car, rickshaw)}', '{(ferry, ferry), (ferry, train), (train, ferry), (train, train), (car, ferry), (car, train)}', 'c', 1, 'Combine each first-stage choice with each second-stage choice.', '1. There are 3 first-stage choices and 2 second-stage choices.
