        ('mth11b-08-mcq-0140', 8, 'Which graphical region solves 7x + 3y ≤ 35, 4x + 1y ≤ 20, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0?', 'the first-quadrant region satisfying both inequalities with > instead of ≤', 'the region above both lines in the first quadrant', 'the whole intersection of the two half-planes without x≥0,y≥0', 'the first-quadrant intersection satisfying 7x+3y≤35 and 4x+1y≤20, including both boundary lines', 'd', 3, 'Graph both boundary lines, shade the ≤ side of each, then intersect with the first quadrant.', 'Correct working:
Each ≤ inequality gives the half-plane on or below its boundary line. x≥0,y≥0 restrict the graph to the first quadrant.
The solution is the common intersection of these regions, with both boundary lines included.
Therefore, the correct answer is the first-quadrant intersection satisfying 7x+3y≤35 and 4x+1y≤20, including both boundary lines.
Option A: reversing one inequality, shading the wrong side, or omitting first-quadrant restrictions.
Option B: reversing one inequality, shading the wrong side, or omitting first-quadrant restrictions.
