        ('mth11b-08-mcq-0146', 8, 'What happens when both sides of an inequality are divided by a negative number?', 'The inequality sign stays unchanged', 'The inequality sign is reversed', 'Both sides become zero', 'The inequality becomes an equation', 'b', 1, 'Recall the special rule for multiplication or division by a negative quantity.', 'Correct working:
Dividing both sides by a negative number reverses > to < or < to >, and similarly for ≥ and ≤.
