        ('mth11b-08-mcq-0149', 8, 'For 2x + 3y ≤ 12, what kind of graph represents the boundary?', 'A dotted line x=6', 'A solid line 2x+3y=12', 'A horizontal line y=12 only', 'No boundary line', 'b', 1, 'Non-strict inequalities include their boundary.', 'Correct working:
The boundary equation is 2x+3y=12. Since ≤ includes equality, the boundary is drawn as a solid line.
