        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0001', 9, 'After a discount of 12% on an article, its price is Rs. 79200. If the discount is increased by 3 percentage points and the new price is Rs. 76500, what was the original price?', 'Rs. 22500', 'Rs. 81900', 'Rs. 86931.82', 'Rs. 90000', 'd', 1, 'Use the difference between the two selling prices as the extra discount amount.', 'The extra discount is Rs. 2700, which represents 3% of the original price. Therefore original price = Rs. 2700 × 100/3 = Rs. 90000.
