        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0061', 9, 'A product passes through a distributor and wholesaler who earn 10% and 15% profit respectively. The total increase from original price to the final selling price is 51.8%. What percentage profit is earned by the retailer?', '26.8%', '41.8%', '32.09%', '20%', 'd', 3, 'Multiply the successive price factors rather than simply adding the percentages.', 'Let the retailer''s rate be x%. Then (1+10/100)(1+15/100)(1+x/100)=1+51.8/100. Therefore 1+x/100=(1+0.518)/[(1+0.1)(1+0.15)], so x=20%.
