        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0062', 9, 'A product passes through a distributor and wholesaler who earn 8% and 12% profit respectively. The total increase from original price to the final selling price is 39%. What percentage profit is earned by the retailer?', '19%', '31%', '14.91%', '24.11%', 'c', 3, 'Multiply the successive price factors rather than simply adding the percentages.', 'Let the retailer''s rate be x%. Then (1+8/100)(1+12/100)(1+x/100)=1+39.0/100. Therefore 1+x/100=(1+0.39)/[(1+0.08)(1+0.12)], so x=14.91%.
