        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0151', 9, 'An asset decreases in value from Rs. 23625 to Rs. 15379 in 3 years at a constant annual depreciation rate. Find the rate of depreciation.', '11.63%', '13.33%', '17.87%', '34.9%', 'b', 3, 'Use A = V(1 − r/100)^n and take the nth-root factor.', 'A/V = 0.65 = (1−r/100)^3. Hence 1−r/100 = (0.65)^(1/3), giving r = 13.33%.
