        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0171', 9, 'Two partners invest in the ratio 10:9. If 5% of the total profit is given to charity and the first partner receives Rs. 2000, what is the total profit?', 'Rs. 3800', 'Rs. 4000', 'Rs. 2105.26', 'Rs. 4444.44', 'b', 2, 'First determine the first partner''s fraction of the profit remaining after charity.', 'After charity, 95% remains. The first partner gets 10/19 of that, so their share is 95×10/19% of total = 50%. Thus total profit = Rs. 2000/0.5 = Rs. 4000.
