        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0172', 9, 'Two partners invest in the ratio 3:2. If 10% of the total profit is given to charity and the first partner receives Rs. 2700, what is the total profit?', 'Rs. 5000', 'Rs. 4500', 'Rs. 3000', 'Rs. 7500', 'a', 2, 'First determine the first partner''s fraction of the profit remaining after charity.', 'After charity, 90% remains. The first partner gets 3/5 of that, so their share is 90×3/5% of total = 54%. Thus total profit = Rs. 2700/0.54 = Rs. 5000.
