        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0190', 9, 'Partners A, B and C begin with investments in the ratio 6:7:9. After six months, A doubles the original investment, B changes to 2 times the original investment and C changes to 4.5 times the original investment. What is their profit ratio at the end of one year?', '6:7:9', '12:14:40.5', '1:1.17:2.75', '18:21:50.5', 'c', 2, 'For each partner, add the capital-time products for the first and second six-month periods.', 'Capital-time totals are proportional to 6+12=18, 7+2×7=21, and 9+4.5×9=49.5. Hence the profit ratio is 18:21:49.5, equivalent to the displayed ratio.
