        ('mth11b-09-mcq-0191', 9, 'Partner A invests Rs. 15000 and partner B invests Rs. 20000. A receives 30% of the total profit for managing the business; the remaining profit is divided in proportion to capital. If total profit is Rs. 100000, how much does each partner receive?', 'A: Rs. 30000, B: Rs. 40000', 'A: Rs. 60000, B: Rs. 40000', 'A: Rs. 30000, B: Rs. 70000', 'A: Rs. 60000, B: Rs. 70000', 'b', 3, 'First remove the management percentage from total profit, then divide the remainder in the capital ratio.', 'Management share = Rs. 30000. Remaining = Rs. 70000. Capital ratio = 15000:20000 = 3:4. A''s capital share of the remainder = Rs. 30000; B''s = Rs. 40000. Therefore A receives Rs. 60000 and B Rs. 40000.
